      "Vimto flavor is essentially UK-only"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "One of the better clear wheys, and the reason people search for Vimto protein powder.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "About 20 g (listing)",
      "Calories": "About 85-90",
      "Third-party testing": "Check certifier database",
      "Best for": "Summer, post-cardio"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "optimum-nutrition-gold-standard-100-whey",
    "name": "Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey",
    "brand": "Optimum Nutrition",
    "badge": "Alternative: Easiest US Buy",
    "category": "Whey isolate + concentrate blend",
    "description": "The best-known whey in the US and the simplest alternative to Myprotein for an Amazon buyer. Per the label at the time of writing, a roughly 30 to 31 g scoop provides about 24 g of protein and 120 calories, with about 3 g of carbohydrate and 1 g of sugar. Optimum Nutrition states it carries Informed Choice certification, and it is sold in many sizes with frequent discounts.",
    "pros": [
      "About 24 g of protein per scoop, per the label",
      "Widely available on Amazon in many sizes",
      "Promoted as Informed Choice certified"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Usually costs more per 25 g than Myprotein on sale",
      "Concentrate in the blend means some lactose"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Buy it instead of Myprotein if you want one predictable tub without chasing codes.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "About 24 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 120",
      "Third-party testing": "Informed Choice (confirm flavor)",
      "Best for": "US Amazon buyers"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "dymatize-iso100-hydrolyzed",
    "name": "Dymatize ISO100 Hydrolyzed Whey Isolate",
    "brand": "Dymatize",
    "badge": "Alternative: Premium Isolate",
    "category": "Hydrolyzed whey isolate + whey isolate",
    "description": "The benchmark US isolate and the natural comparison for Impact Whey Isolate. Per the label at the time of writing, a 30 g scoop delivers 25 g of protein in about 110 to 120 calories, with roughly 1 g of sugar and very little lactose. Dymatize describes it as banned-substance tested, and it is sold widely on Amazon and in grocery chains.",
    "pros": [
      "25 g of protein per scoop, per the label",
      "Very low lactose, fat and carbohydrate",
      "Thin, quick mix in water, per buyer reports"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Premium cost per 25 g of protein",
      "Sucralose and stevia in flavored versions"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The isolate to buy if you want the most predictable label and will pay more for it.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "About 25 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 110-120",
      "Third-party testing": "Banned-substance tested, per brand",
      "Best for": "Lactose-sensitive, cutting"
    }
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/best-of/`,
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Myprotein Review",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/myprotein-review/`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Myprotein a good brand?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes for value-focused buyers. Myprotein makes straightforward whey products with honest labels, a huge flavor range and frequent discounts that often make it among the cheapest mainstream whey per gram of protein. Its weaknesses are a small Impact Whey scoop, prices that depend on discount codes and differences between countries. It is owned by THG PLC, a UK company listed in London."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much protein is in Myprotein Impact Whey?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A 25 g scoop of Impact Whey Protein provides roughly 20 to 22 g of protein, depending on flavor and market, per label figures at the time of writing. Unflavored sits at the higher end. To reach 25 g of protein you need about 30 g of powder. The US Impact Whey Isolate lists about 25 g of protein per scoop."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you buy Myprotein on Amazon US?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, partly. Impact Whey Isolate is listed on Amazon US, sold by Myprotein North America and shipped by Amazon, and Clear Whey Isolate is also listed. The classic Impact Whey Protein concentrate did not appear as a brand-sold Amazon US listing when we checked, so buy that one from Myprotein's US site, ideally during a sale."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Vimto protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is Myprotein Clear Whey Isolate in a licensed Vimto flavor, based on the British fruit cordial. UK listings show about 20 g of protein and around 89 calories per roughly 26 g serving, sweetened with sucralose. It is sold through Myprotein and UK retailers such as Sainsbury's, Boots and Costco UK, and is hard to find from brand-authorized sellers in the US."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Myprotein Impact Whey good for weight loss?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can help because it adds protein for relatively few calories, roughly 90 to 105 per 25 g scoop, which supports fullness and muscle retention in a calorie deficit. Impact Whey Isolate is slightly leaner still. Protein powder only supports weight loss as part of an overall deficit, and it should not replace whole meals for long periods."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Myprotein third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Some Myprotein products carry the Informed Choice mark, including UK listings for Impact Whey Isolate. Coverage varies by product, flavor and country, so tested athletes should look up the exact product in the Informed Choice or Informed Sport database. We could not find batch heavy-metal reports published by the brand."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Myprotein better than Optimum Nutrition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Neither is better across the board. Myprotein is usually cheaper per 25 g of protein on sale and offers more flavors and formats. Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard gives about 24 g of protein per scoop, is widely available on Amazon and is promoted as Informed Choice certified, which makes it the simpler choice for many US buyers."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: SITE_NAME, url: SITE_URL },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.brand ?? product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "myprotein",
      "my protein",
      "my protein powder",
      "myprotein impact whey",
      "myprotein review",
      "vimto protein powder"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Whey Protein Picks",
    link: "/best-whey-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Brand Review
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Label-Checked
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Myprotein <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Myprotein is the UK's best-known budget whey brand and sells across the US too. Here is which product in the range to buy, why the scoop size matters more than the headline number, and who should buy a different brand.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#myprotein-impact-whey-isolate"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#impact-whey"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Which One to Buy
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">{author.name}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">{author.role}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Verdict</a>
          <a href="#who-owns-it" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Who Owns Myprotein</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. The Range, Ranked</a>
          <a href="#impact-whey" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Impact Whey Label</a>
          <a href="#isolate-vs-concentrate" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Whey vs Isolate</a>
          <a href="#clear-whey" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Clear Whey and Vimto</a>
          <a href="#cost" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Cost per 25 g</a>
          <a href="#testing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Testing and Trust</a>
          <a href="#vs-us-brands" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Myprotein vs US Brands</a>
          <a href="#who-should-skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Who Should Skip It</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Myprotein is good value, not magic. Its Impact Whey is a perfectly decent whey concentrate that is often among the cheapest mainstream powders per gram of protein when it is on sale, which is most of the time. The catch is the scoop: a 25 g serving delivers roughly 20 to 22 g of protein, so you need a bigger scoop than the label suggests, and the product you can actually buy on Amazon US is the isolate, not the famous concentrate.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Is Myprotein Any Good? The Short Verdict
          </h2>

          <p>
            Yes, for the right buyer. Myprotein makes straightforward whey products with reasonable labels, an enormous flavor range and prices that, with the near-permanent discount codes, are often among the lowest per gram of protein of any mainstream brand. Its flagship Impact Whey Protein carries a 4.6-star average from more than 30,000 reviews on the brand's own site, which says something about how many people keep buying it.
          </p>

          <p>
            The weaknesses are just as clear. The standard Impact Whey scoop is small, so the protein per serving looks low next to US brands. The product you can find most easily on Amazon US is the isolate, which is a better powder but not the cheap concentrate that made the brand famous. And list prices are deliberately inflated so that discounts look large, which makes price comparisons harder than they should be.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our ranking is simple. If you are in the US and want to buy on Amazon, buy <strong>Impact Whey Isolate</strong>. If you are happy to order from Myprotein's own site during a sale, <strong>Impact Whey Protein</strong> is the value pick. If you want a light, juice-style drink instead of a milkshake, <strong>Clear Whey Isolate</strong> is one of the better clear wheys available, and in the UK the Vimto flavor is the one people search for by name.
          </p>

          <p>
            Who should skip it? Anyone who is lactose sensitive and considering the concentrate, anyone who needs a named sport certification on the exact tub they buy, and anyone who hates chasing discount codes. For those readers, US brands such as Optimum Nutrition and Dymatize offer a more predictable buying experience, and our <a href="/best-whey-protein-powder/">best whey protein powder</a> roundup ranks the wider field.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-owns-it" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Who Owns Myprotein and Where It Sells
          </h2>

          <p>
            Myprotein is owned by <strong>THG PLC</strong>, the Manchester-based group listed on the London Stock Exchange, and it sits inside THG's nutrition division, THG Nutrition. In April 2025 THG's board publicly rejected an unsolicited proposal from Selkirk to buy Myprotein that put a headline value of 400 to 600 million pounds on the brand, so it remains part of THG. In its Q3 trading statement in October 2026, THG raised its earnings forecast, citing stronger performance in THG Nutrition.
          </p>

          <p>
            That ownership explains the business model. Myprotein sells mostly direct, through country-specific websites, with retail and marketplace listings layered on top. Direct selling is what allows the constant sales: the brand captures the margin a retailer would otherwise take, then spends part of it on discount codes. It also explains why prices and formulas differ between the UK, US and other markets.
          </p>

          <p>
            In the US, Myprotein runs its own site and an Amazon presence. The Impact Whey Isolate listing we checked on Amazon US is sold by Myprotein North America and shipped by Amazon, which is the arrangement you want for authenticity. The Clear Whey Isolate is also listed on Amazon US. The classic Impact Whey Protein concentrate, however, did not appear as a brand-sold listing on Amazon US when we checked, so the buy button on that card runs a search rather than pointing to a single listing.
          </p>

          <p>
            In the UK, Myprotein is everywhere: its own site, supermarkets such as Sainsbury's and Morrisons, Boots, Holland and Barrett and Costco. That retail reach is why UK-only flavors such as Vimto Clear Whey are so visible in search. If you are shopping on Amazon in the US and want to compare more options, our <a href="/amazon-protein-powder/">guide to buying protein powder on Amazon</a> explains how to check the seller before you pay.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. The Myprotein Range, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            Three Myprotein powders cover almost everything most buyers need, followed by two US alternatives for readers who would rather buy a brand with a bigger scoop or an easier Amazon listing. Label figures come from Myprotein, Amazon US and retailer listings at the time of writing and vary by flavor and by market, so check the panel on your tub.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-[#FF4500] text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-black">
                      {index + 1}
                    </span>
                    {productImages[product.id] && (
                      <img
                        src={productImages[product.id]}
                        alt={product.name}
                        loading="lazy"
                        width="40"
                        height="40"
                        class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-white object-contain p-1 shrink-0"
                      />
                    )}
                    <div>
                      <p class="text-white font-black text-lg">{product.name}</p>
                      <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#38BDF8]/20 text-[#38BDF8] px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold hidden sm:block">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  {product.rating && (
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
                    <div class="flex text-yellow-400">
                      {[...Array(5)].map((_, i) => (
                        <svg
                          class={`w-4 h-4 ${i < Math.floor(product.rating) ? "fill-current" : "text-gray-200"}`}
                          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                          viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                          fill="currentColor"
                        >
                          <path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z" />
                        </svg>
                      ))}
